A03.text:
Under para 20 of the Know Your Customer Directions, 2025, an NBFC shall undertake risk categorisation based on parameters such as:
- The customer’s identity, social / financial status, nature of business activity, and information about the customer’s business and its location [1][2];
- Geographical risk covering customers as well as transactions [1][2];
- Type of products / services offered, and the delivery channel used for delivery of products / services [1][2];
- Types of transactions undertaken such as cash, cheque / monetary instruments, wire transfers, forex transactions, etc. [2].

The NBFC may also factor in the ability to confirm identity documents through online or other services offered by issuing authorities while considering the customer’s identity [2].
